                     "year": "1884",
                     "month": "",
                     "day": ""
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection: That's all?</b><br /><br />Were there only 25 nations in the world in <htdate0>?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "1884",
                     "month": "",
                     "day": ""
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "Unlike in <htdate0>, when not all nations were represented, today every country approves the International Reference Meridian. This is the imaginary line that wraps around the Earth. It runs 102.5 meters (336 feet) from the old reference line, the Airy Meridian — the fourth meridian created by the British (<htcite0>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "9828a108-dfdf-4692-a819-18b690d4a629",
                     "text": "Raikar, S.P.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "12",
                        "day": "22"
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": [
                  {
                     "type": "gregory",
                     "year": "1884",
                     "month": "",
                     "day": ""
                  }
               ],
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "#### A central idea\n\nAs we saw at the start of this text, China (Zhongguo 中國) has held the idea of being the center for about 3,000 years. So the definition set in <htdate0> simply ignored this age-old understanding.\n\nOn the other hand, when China (Zhongguo 中國) accepts the International Reference Meridian (<htcite0>), the nation does not lose its identity.\n\nWhat looks like a contradiction has in fact been normal for the Chinese for centuries. It points to a broader idea. Look at the map at the top of this section, made by the Jesuit Matteo Ricci while he lived among the Chinese. It shows the 17th-century world by the Gregorian calendar, with China (Zhongguo 中國) at the center and a role much like Europe's (<htcite1>).\n\nIn that light, nothing has changed for China (Zhongguo 中國).\n\n#### Let us be centered\n\nMaps are never fully neutral (<htcite2>), but we will try anyway. Look at today's world map in the Mercator projection — the kind often used in Western books — in **Figure 2**:",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "9828a108-dfdf-4692-a819-18b690d4a629",
                     "text": "Raikar, S.P.",
                     "page": "",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "12",
                        "day": "22"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "59b80e45-89fe-437f-b4b2-fc191b1e7d14",
                     "text": "Kästl, M.",
                     "page": "pp. 231- 234, 242 - 247",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2024",
                        "month": "12",
                        "day": "22"
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "59b80e45-89fe-437f-b4b2-fc191b1e7d14",
                     "text": "Kästl, M.",
                     "page": "pp. 242",
